another day another protest in panama  thousands of people marched once again  to demand measures to curb inflation and  corruption in the central american  country they've been out on the streets  almost daily for the past two  the weeks situation in panama is  unlivable there are no medical supplies  there are salary cuts and there's no  work there's no money to pay doctors as  a student the future worries me a lot  on wednesday indigenous groups joined  teachers students and other unions in  the demonstrations promising to further  deepen the crisis  we call on the president of the republic  to heed our request if he does not  respond to our petition we will mobilize  the indigenous territories of panama  on monday president laurentino cortiso  announced a reduction in the price of  fuel now the government has presented a  decree controlling the price of 10 basic  food items among them lentils and  vegetable oil  it also promised to slash government  public spending by 10 percent  but for protesters these measures don't  go far enough  hotdog vendor jose gonzalez says the  situation is the worst he's seen in  decades  with the rise in fuel costs everything  became more expensive the bread the hot  dogs and not sensemore it has doubled in  23 years doing this job i'd never seen  so many people working informally on the  streets i don't think the government is  offering real solutions  solutions that panamanians are becoming  increasingly impatient for alessandra  ampietti al jazeera
 

